<p>Albuquerque does not get much national hype, and that works in your favor. Rent and everyday costs are lower than in Denver, Phoenix or anywhere on the coast, film and TV studios keep production crews busy, and the city hosts one of the most photographed events on Earth every October. Put those together and the best side hustles in Albuquerque can pay far more than the local wage scale suggests.</p>
<p>This guide breaks down 17 side gigs that work in the Duke City, what each typically pays, what it costs to start, and the New Mexico-specific rules, especially gross receipts tax, that catch many first-time side hustlers off guard.</p>

