<h2 id="what-drives-demand">What drives side income in Albuquerque</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Film and television.</strong> Netflix and NBCUniversal operate studios in the metro, and New Mexico's production incentives draw a steady stream of shows and films. Sets need background actors, drivers, production assistants and local services.</li>
  <li><strong>Big, stable employers.</strong> Sandia National Laboratories, Kirtland Air Force Base, the University of New Mexico, Presbyterian Healthcare and Intel in Rio Rancho bring in well-paid professionals who outsource chores and tutoring.</li>
  <li><strong>A signature event calendar.</strong> The Albuquerque International Balloon Fiesta in early October, the Gathering of Nations powwow in spring, the New Mexico State Fair in September, plus Isotopes baseball and New Mexico United soccer.</li>
  <li><strong>High-desert seasons.</strong> Spring winds, summer monsoons, chile-roasting season in late summer and the occasional winter snowfall each bring their own short bursts of work.</li>
</ul>

